<section class="content">

<h2>Catechist's Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For class preparation and delivery. For the catechist's use only.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Central theme:</strong> God reveals himself as Trinity &mdash; one God in three Persons &mdash; and this mystery is the heart of the Christian faith and of our lives.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Understand that the Trinity is the central mystery of the Christian faith, not an advanced or secondary topic.</li>
<li>Know how God progressively revealed himself as Trinity in the history of salvation.</li>
<li>Distinguish that the divine Persons are truly distinct but share the same divine nature.</li>
<li>Internalize that &laquo;God is Love&raquo; (1 Jn 4:8) is the key to understanding the Trinity.</li>
<li>Live the Christian life as an invitation to enter into Trinitarian communion.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> &laquo;The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ, the love of God, and the fellowship of the Holy Spirit be with you all&raquo; (2 Cor 13:13)</p>
<p><strong>CCC references:</strong> 232-267</p>

</section>

